    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "An early ranch in Dibble served as a stopping point for soldiers and travelers on the Fort Smith to Fort Sill military road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dibble%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village of Dibble may have existed as early as 1869, with a post office established there by 1894.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dibble%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ranching and farming served as the early economic staples for the community of Dibble.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dibble%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dibble lost many of its early businesses in 1906 after the Oklahoma Central Railway bypassed the town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dibble%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Dibble Creek drains the center and northern parts of town, flowing east to join Walnut Creek.",
